1
00:00:15,100 --> 00:00:16,877
Destiny. Fate. Dreams.

2
00:00:16,960 --> 00:00:21,140
These unstoppable ideals are
held deep in the heart of man.

3
00:00:21,560 --> 00:00:24,972
As long as there are people
who seek freedom in this life,

4
00:00:25,060 --> 00:00:27,707
these things shall not
vanish from the earth.

5
00:00:34,720 --> 00:00:37,497
People tell me my head's in the clouds.

6
00:00:37,580 --> 00:00:40,897
I don't care what they say
because I'm dreaming of you.

7
00:00:40,980 --> 00:00:43,557
You are the treasure I found.

8
00:00:43,640 --> 00:00:46,657
So bright, so bold, and so elusive.

9
00:00:46,740 --> 00:00:48,737
It's hard to look away.

10
00:00:48,820 --> 00:00:51,837
Even though it's blinding me.

11
00:00:51,920 --> 00:00:55,697
There are no words to
describe how I feel inside.

12
00:00:55,780 --> 00:00:58,000
I'm really, really stuck on you.

13
00:00:59,220 --> 00:01:02,537
I have to follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

14
00:01:02,620 --> 00:01:05,597
And I won't stop till I
get there, you will see.

15
00:01:05,680 --> 00:01:08,897
You're all I need to have
the strength to believe.

16
00:01:08,980 --> 00:01:11,000
Believe in wonder.

17
00:01:17,840 --> 00:01:21,117
I'm gonna follow my dreams,
however crazy they seem.

18
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:24,157
I'm gonna share them
with you, a love so true.

19
00:01:24,240 --> 00:01:27,557
You're all I want,
together we can move on.

20
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:29,917
We live how we want to.

21
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,037
There is no limit to us.

22
00:01:32,120 --> 00:01:33,537
We have the power of love.

23
00:01:33,620 --> 00:01:36,617
We don't want to live ordinary lives.

24
00:01:36,700 --> 00:01:39,777
We have a chance to live in paradise.

25
00:01:39,860 --> 00:01:42,480
We live in one another.

26
00:01:54,340 --> 00:01:55,170
Vivi!

27
00:01:57,760 --> 00:02:00,080
Who are you?!

28
00:02:01,080 --> 00:02:02,560
Ready? Aim!

29
00:02:08,840 --> 00:02:10,200
No! Stop it!

30
00:02:10,380 --> 00:02:12,637
Fighting is not going to help anything!

31
00:02:12,720 --> 00:02:13,880
I'm fine, Luffy.

32
00:02:14,020 --> 00:02:15,314
It only grazed my arm.

33
00:02:18,420 --> 00:02:19,250
It's alright.

34
00:02:19,333 --> 00:02:20,300
We won't land.

35
00:02:20,540 --> 00:02:22,658
But can you please call us a doctor?

36
00:02:23,360 --> 00:02:26,900
Our friend is dying from a
serious illness. I'm begging you.

37
00:02:27,180 --> 00:02:28,300
Please help us.

38
00:02:29,340 --> 00:02:30,170
Vivi.

39
00:02:30,253 --> 00:02:33,376
You are not fit to be the
captain of this ship, Luffy.

40
00:02:33,820 --> 00:02:37,114
Not everything can be fixed
by rushing to start a fight.

41
00:02:39,860 --> 00:02:41,720
We can't get into a fight here.

42
00:02:42,080 --> 00:02:43,080
Think about Nami.

43
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:44,671
What would happen to her?

44
00:02:52,680 --> 00:02:56,437
Yeah right I'm sorry about that please

45
00:02:56,520 --> 00:03:00,840
help us call a doctor
our friend needs you!

46
00:03:06,520 --> 00:03:09,520
I'll show you to our village follow me.

47
00:03:16,180 --> 00:03:17,010
See?

48
00:03:17,093 --> 00:03:20,360
Just ask politely Yeah,
you're incredible, Vivi!

49
00:03:29,060 --> 00:03:31,657
There is one thing I feel I
should warn you about, though!

50
00:03:31,740 --> 00:03:34,057
The only doctor we have
here is actually a witch.

51
00:03:34,140 --> 00:03:34,970
Huh?

52
00:03:35,053 --> 00:03:35,883
A witch?

53
00:03:36,180 --> 00:03:39,897
You've got to be kidding me Everything
about this island is messed up.

54
00:03:39,980 --> 00:03:42,804
What do you people call
this weird place anyway?

55
00:03:43,760 --> 00:03:46,097
Actually, this land still
doesn't have a name.

56
00:03:46,180 --> 00:03:47,660
An island without a name?

57
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:49,882
I didn't know that was possible.

58
00:03:50,200 --> 00:03:52,040
A bear!

59
00:03:53,120 --> 00:03:53,950
Hurry, everyone!

60
00:03:54,033 --> 00:03:54,998
Pretend to be dead!

61
00:03:57,320 --> 00:03:58,520
A hiking bear.

62
00:03:58,660 --> 00:03:59,778
He poses no threat.

63
00:04:00,320 --> 00:04:01,560
Don't forget to bow.

64
00:04:01,900 --> 00:04:03,076
It's proper manners.

65
00:04:09,020 --> 00:04:09,850
Nice.

66
00:04:09,933 --> 00:04:10,998
That's much better.

67
00:04:14,580 --> 00:04:17,197
Now I can finally get back
to some real training.

68
00:04:17,280 --> 00:04:21,717
I was getting sick of that modified training
that I had to do with my stupid injury.

69
00:04:21,800 --> 00:04:24,741
Besides, just watching the
ship is boring as hell.

70
00:04:26,140 --> 00:04:29,846
Maybe some ice water swimming
will help me clear my head a bit.

71
00:04:34,760 --> 00:04:36,760
This is the village where we live.

72
00:04:37,020 --> 00:04:38,240
Its name is Bighorn.

73
00:04:39,020 --> 00:04:41,817
Look at all the weird animals
walking around everywhere.

74
00:04:41,900 --> 00:04:43,488
Yeah, this is snow country.

75
00:04:43,720 --> 00:04:46,617
Look, Nami, we've made it
to a village with people.

76
00:04:46,700 --> 00:04:47,560
We're here.

77
00:04:48,720 --> 00:04:50,485
Thanks for the help, everyone.

78
00:04:51,160 --> 00:04:53,757
If you're not a guard, you
can return to your work.

79
00:04:53,840 --> 00:04:56,517
Are you completely certain that
you'll be all right here by yourself?

80
00:04:56,600 --> 00:04:57,680
They are pirates.

81
00:04:58,200 --> 00:05:00,494
I believe these people mean us no harm.

82
00:05:00,880 --> 00:05:02,233
That's my hunch anyway.

83
00:05:02,540 --> 00:05:03,977
You can trust me on that.

84
00:05:04,060 --> 00:05:05,317
So what should we do now?

85
00:05:05,400 --> 00:05:07,077
They're all right then I
think we should believe

86
00:05:07,160 --> 00:05:09,866
it they do seem to be
pretty harmless huh yeah

87
00:05:10,660 --> 00:05:15,797
All right Dalton we'll leave them
to you even so be careful Dalton and

88
00:05:15,880 --> 00:05:21,657
call us again if you need Anything
you mean those men weren't your land

89
00:05:21,740 --> 00:05:26,337
security forces no they're just ordinary
citizens Come to my house for now

90
00:05:26,420 --> 00:05:32,257
hey look over there Loopy it's one of those
hiking bears another one Hello, Dalton.

91
00:05:32,340 --> 00:05:34,497
I heard that some pirates
landed on the island.

92
00:05:34,580 --> 00:05:36,057
I hope everything is all right.

93
00:05:36,140 --> 00:05:37,493
Yes, everything's fine.

94
00:05:37,740 --> 00:05:39,858
There's nothing to be worried about.

95
00:05:40,700 --> 00:05:45,017
Just want you to know, Dalton, I'm looking
forward to the election in two days.

96
00:05:45,100 --> 00:05:47,837
Everyone I've talked to has said
they're going to vote for you.

97
00:05:47,920 --> 00:05:50,057
I'm sure you're not serious about that.

98
00:05:50,140 --> 00:05:52,552
I'm just an ordinary citizen, that's all.

99
00:05:58,840 --> 00:06:00,657
You can use that bed over there.

100
00:06:00,740 --> 00:06:02,564
I'm going to warm the place up.

101
00:06:05,960 --> 00:06:07,897
I guess I should introduce myself.

102
00:06:07,980 --> 00:06:08,810
My name is Dalton.

103
00:06:08,893 --> 00:06:11,237
I'm the captain of the
island's security squad.

104
00:06:11,320 --> 00:06:14,026
Please forgive our less
than friendly welcome.

105
00:06:14,640 --> 00:06:16,737
Excuse me, but may I ask you a question?

106
00:06:16,820 --> 00:06:17,650
Huh?

107
00:06:17,733 --> 00:06:20,635
It's just that you look
familiar to me for some reason.

108
00:06:21,060 --> 00:06:23,660
No, I just have one of
those faces, I guess.

109
00:06:24,320 --> 00:06:28,557
Anyway, can you tell us more about this
doctor, or witch, if that's what she is?

110
00:06:28,640 --> 00:06:30,440
Nami's fever's gone up to 107.

111
00:06:31,620 --> 00:06:33,032
How long has she had it?

112
00:06:33,400 --> 00:06:36,237
It's been several days, and
it just keeps getting higher.

113
00:06:36,320 --> 00:06:37,150
I see.

114
00:06:37,233 --> 00:06:39,157
She'll likely die if it gets any worse.

115
00:06:39,240 --> 00:06:43,337
Yes, but we have no idea what the
illness is, much less how to treat it.

116
00:06:43,420 --> 00:06:44,797
We don't know how to help her.

117
00:06:44,880 --> 00:06:47,477
We've got to find a doctor
as soon as possible.

118
00:06:47,560 --> 00:06:48,617
Any doctor will do.

119
00:06:48,700 --> 00:06:49,837
Where is this witch of yours?

120
00:06:49,920 --> 00:06:50,750
The witch?

121
00:06:50,840 --> 00:06:53,546
Do you see those mountains
outside the window?

122
00:06:53,680 --> 00:06:55,720
Yeah, I noticed them earlier.

123
00:06:57,320 --> 00:06:58,555
Supermassive Snowman!

124
00:06:58,720 --> 00:07:00,661
And the feared Snowbeast Nozilla!

125
00:07:02,160 --> 00:07:04,000
Get in here before I kill you!

126
00:07:06,540 --> 00:07:09,757
Those mountains out there are
known as the Drum Rockies.

127
00:07:09,840 --> 00:07:10,760
Look closely.

128
00:07:11,140 --> 00:07:14,397
Do you see the castle on top of the
tallest one, the one in the middle?

129
00:07:14,480 --> 00:07:15,310
Castle?

130
00:07:15,520 --> 00:07:18,137
That castle has lost its key. Much warmer.

131
00:07:18,220 --> 00:07:19,980
Yeah, I see it up there.

132
00:07:20,380 --> 00:07:22,437
What's so important about the castle?

133
00:07:22,520 --> 00:07:26,460
That castle is where our lands
only doctor lives. Dr. Kureha.

134
00:07:27,040 --> 00:07:29,217
She's the one who people
here call a witch.

135
00:07:29,300 --> 00:07:30,130
What?

136
00:07:30,213 --> 00:07:33,097
Of all places, why does she have
to live on top of a mountain?

137
00:07:33,180 --> 00:07:34,977
We need to call her here right now.

138
00:07:35,060 --> 00:07:36,236
Nami needs her help.

139
00:07:36,460 --> 00:07:39,337
I'm sorry, but I'm afraid
there's no way to contact her.

140
00:07:39,420 --> 00:07:40,860
You can't be serious!

141
00:07:41,180 --> 00:07:42,757
What kind of a doctor is she?

142
00:07:42,840 --> 00:07:45,597
Her skills as a doctor are
quite impressive, actually.

143
00:07:45,680 --> 00:07:47,397
However, she's an eccentric old woman.

144
00:07:47,480 --> 00:07:49,900
She's nearly 140 years old now.

145
00:07:50,940 --> 00:07:52,340
A hundred and forty?

146
00:07:52,640 --> 00:07:54,357
No wonder she doesn't get around much.

147
00:07:54,440 --> 00:07:55,557
Oh, and one more thing.

148
00:07:55,640 --> 00:07:57,052
She likes pickled plums.

149
00:07:57,460 --> 00:07:59,817
What happens when people
here get sick or injured?

150
00:07:59,900 --> 00:08:01,037
Doesn't she help them?

151
00:08:01,120 --> 00:08:03,817
She comes down from the mountain
whenever she feels like it.

152
00:08:03,900 --> 00:08:05,457
She looks around for patients.

153
00:08:05,540 --> 00:08:06,437
She treats them.

154
00:08:06,520 --> 00:08:11,017
And before she leaves, she takes whatever
she wants from their houses as payment.

155
00:08:11,100 --> 00:08:13,277
She doesn't sound like a very nice lady.

156
00:08:13,360 --> 00:08:15,595
It kind of sounds like she's a pirate.

157
00:08:15,800 --> 00:08:19,917
But how is a woman as old as she is
capable of getting down that mountain?

158
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:21,765
It's an odd rumor around here.

159
00:08:22,380 --> 00:08:25,017
But several of the villagers
claim they've seen her at night,

160
00:08:25,100 --> 00:08:27,697
riding a sleigh of some
kind through the sky.

161
00:08:27,780 --> 00:08:30,427
They see her silhouette
when the moon is out.

162
00:08:31,840 --> 00:08:34,605
That's the reason she is
thought to be a witch.

163
00:08:35,480 --> 00:08:38,637
There are others who say they've
seen her with a strange creature.

164
00:08:38,720 --> 00:08:40,937
A creature that none of them recognize.

165
00:08:41,020 --> 00:08:43,240
See! I knew it! A snow monster!

166
00:08:43,380 --> 00:08:45,157
Where there's snow, there's
gotta be snow monsters!

167
00:08:45,240 --> 00:08:46,317
Oh, I knew there'd be one!

168
00:08:49,480 --> 00:08:51,186
I don't want to run into one!

169
00:08:52,540 --> 00:08:53,370
Dr.

170
00:08:53,453 --> 00:08:54,957
Kureha is the only doctor we have,

171
00:08:55,040 --> 00:08:57,937
but she's still a woman I
would prefer to stay away from.

172
00:08:58,020 --> 00:09:01,957
All we can do is wait for the next time
she decides to come down the mountain.

173
00:09:02,040 --> 00:09:02,870
Really?

174
00:09:03,300 --> 00:09:04,300
No, damn it.

175
00:09:04,460 --> 00:09:06,397
We can't wait here for that long.

176
00:09:06,480 --> 00:09:08,597
Nami is getting even worse as we speak.

177
00:09:08,680 --> 00:09:10,160
Hey, Nami! Nami!

178
00:09:10,380 --> 00:09:11,300
Wake up now!

179
00:09:11,500 --> 00:09:12,500
Luffy, you idiot!

180
00:09:12,620 --> 00:09:14,208
What are you doing to her?!

181
00:09:16,500 --> 00:09:17,980
Hey, look, she's awake.

182
00:09:18,840 --> 00:09:19,670
Here's the thing.

183
00:09:19,753 --> 00:09:22,017
The only way to see the doctor
is to climb the mountain.

184
00:09:22,100 --> 00:09:24,057
So we're going to have
to climb the mountain.

185
00:09:24,140 --> 00:09:24,997
Are you crazy?

186
00:09:25,080 --> 00:09:25,910
What about Nami?

187
00:09:25,993 --> 00:09:27,537
How do you expect to get her up there?

188
00:09:27,620 --> 00:09:28,450
Easy.

189
00:09:28,533 --> 00:09:29,363
She'll ride on my back.

190
00:09:29,446 --> 00:09:31,677
That's only going to
make her even more sick.

191
00:09:31,760 --> 00:09:32,797
What's the problem?

192
00:09:32,880 --> 00:09:34,397
I thought we needed to hurry.

193
00:09:34,480 --> 00:09:36,557
We do, but you'll never make it up there.

194
00:09:36,640 --> 00:09:38,617
Look at how steep and tall that thing is.

195
00:09:38,700 --> 00:09:39,600
I can do it.

196
00:09:39,740 --> 00:09:42,957
Maybe you can, but climbing that
thing would be way too hard on Nami.

197
00:09:43,040 --> 00:09:46,157
But look, even if we fall or
something, we'll land in snow.

198
00:09:46,240 --> 00:09:47,177
That doesn't matter.

199
00:09:47,260 --> 00:09:49,657
A fall like that would
kill even a healthy person.

200
00:09:49,740 --> 00:09:52,387
Seriously, Luffy, she
has a really bad fever.

201
00:09:52,500 --> 00:09:54,382
It's so high she's almost dying.

202
00:09:54,520 --> 00:09:56,049
Don't you understand that?

203
00:10:01,480 --> 00:10:04,009
I need to get over this
thing, and quickly.

204
00:10:07,120 --> 00:10:09,640
We need to hurry for Vivi.

205
00:10:14,920 --> 00:10:17,000
Come on, Captain. Let's go.

206
00:10:20,740 --> 00:10:22,197
That's what I'm talking about!

207
00:10:22,280 --> 00:10:23,162
Leave it to me!

208
00:10:25,480 --> 00:10:26,980
I can't believe this!

209
00:10:27,160 --> 00:10:29,748
Now our navigator's as
crazy as our captain!

210
00:10:29,960 --> 00:10:32,537
You know, you're in no shape
for a trip like this, Nami.

211
00:10:32,620 --> 00:10:33,837
Are you sure you'll be okay?

212
00:10:33,920 --> 00:10:35,377
It'll take you hours to get there.

213
00:10:35,460 --> 00:10:37,457
Hey, old guy, give me
some meat for the road!

214
00:10:37,540 --> 00:10:38,370
Meat?

215
00:10:39,620 --> 00:10:42,140
Right, I'm coming too. Listen, Luffy.

216
00:10:42,500 --> 00:10:43,660
Be very careful.

217
00:10:43,800 --> 00:10:46,417
You can't fall even once
or Nami is going to die.

218
00:10:46,500 --> 00:10:47,600
Not even once.

219
00:10:47,880 --> 00:10:48,997
Hold still a second.

220
00:10:49,080 --> 00:10:51,374
I need to make sure that this is tight.

221
00:10:51,940 --> 00:10:53,137
Okay, you're all set.

222
00:10:53,220 --> 00:10:54,717
I'm going to wait for you here.

223
00:10:54,800 --> 00:10:57,277
If I came with you guys,
I'd only get in the way.

224
00:10:57,360 --> 00:10:58,190
Yep, me too.

225
00:10:59,400 --> 00:11:00,230
All right.

226
00:11:00,313 --> 00:11:02,507
Now you just hold on
tight to me, okay, Nami?

227
00:11:04,880 --> 00:11:06,527
I guess you're set on going.

228
00:11:07,020 --> 00:11:08,497
I'm not going to try to stop you,

229
00:11:08,580 --> 00:11:10,957
but I will ask you to at least
climb up from the other side.

230
00:11:11,040 --> 00:11:13,957
That way you can avoid the
loppins that are on this side.

231
00:11:14,040 --> 00:11:16,099
They're fierce carnivorous rabbits.

232
00:11:16,480 --> 00:11:18,737
If you run into a pack of
them, you're as good as dead.

233
00:11:18,820 --> 00:11:19,840
Huh? Really?

234
00:11:20,240 --> 00:11:21,697
We've gotta get up there.

235
00:11:21,780 --> 00:11:23,309
We'll be just fine, right?

236
00:11:23,760 --> 00:11:24,880
Yeah, fine.

237
00:11:25,200 --> 00:11:26,440
You can't be serious!

238
00:11:26,800 --> 00:11:28,737
Do you know how easily
those things can kill you?

239
00:11:28,820 --> 00:11:30,077
Nah, we'll be alright.

240
00:11:30,160 --> 00:11:32,660
Now hurry it up, Sanji, before Nami dies!

241
00:11:33,840 --> 00:11:35,857
Don't say stuff like that, you idiot!

242
00:11:35,940 --> 00:11:37,175
Do you wanna Jango us?

243
00:11:40,040 --> 00:11:41,737
Are you sure they'll be all right?

244
00:11:41,820 --> 00:11:45,055
Well, it's not really those
two we need to worry about.

245
00:11:45,440 --> 00:11:46,797
Nami's the one in trouble.

246
00:11:46,880 --> 00:11:49,117
I just hope her strength
can hold out long enough.

247
00:11:49,200 --> 00:11:51,259
She's getting sicker by the minute.

248
00:11:57,500 --> 00:11:59,088
Why are you standing there?

249
00:11:59,620 --> 00:12:00,560
Come on inside.

250
00:12:00,840 --> 00:12:01,958
It's cold out here.

251
00:12:02,340 --> 00:12:03,897
Oh, no, that's really okay.

252
00:12:03,980 --> 00:12:06,140
I want to stay out here. Me too.

253
00:12:12,180 --> 00:12:13,010
I see.

254
00:12:19,380 --> 00:12:21,380
Well, in that case, I'll join you.

255
00:12:26,400 --> 00:12:29,459
We did once have some here
on this island, you know.

256
00:12:30,400 --> 00:12:31,260
Some doctors.

257
00:12:31,620 --> 00:12:35,149
However, all of them left some
time ago for certain reasons.

