handle something like that.

513
00:24:55,600 --> 00:24:56,835
It would be too much.

514
00:24:58,580 --> 00:24:59,700
She could die.

515
00:25:00,780 --> 00:25:01,610
What?

516
00:25:02,600 --> 00:25:05,129
Jeez, okay, then I
won't fight them at all.

517
00:25:05,820 --> 00:25:06,860
But then...

518
00:25:07,600 --> 00:25:09,680
What can I do, huh?

519
00:25:10,160 --> 00:25:11,120
Just dodge!

520
00:25:12,480 --> 00:25:13,940
Dodge, dodge and run!

521
00:25:14,240 --> 00:25:15,520
But don't retreat!

522
00:25:15,820 --> 00:25:17,349
That's a little difficult!

523
00:25:26,260 --> 00:25:30,260
In this snow I can't get my footing
well enough to land a solid kick

524
00:25:43,720 --> 00:25:45,397
Go left, we'll head to the mountain.

525
00:25:45,480 --> 00:25:47,657
Okay, you need to get
rid of them somehow Wow,

526
00:25:47,740 --> 00:25:51,217
it would take us hours to fight them
all off, but how do we shake them now?

527
00:25:51,300 --> 00:25:53,300
For bunnies, these guys are tough.

528
00:25:53,420 --> 00:25:54,420
We're in trouble.

529
00:25:56,220 --> 00:25:57,050
Stop it!

530
00:26:00,440 --> 00:26:01,558
What are you doing?

531
00:26:01,780 --> 00:26:03,777
I told you not to attack, you idiot.

532
00:26:03,860 --> 00:26:05,154
Just leave them to me.

533
00:26:05,460 --> 00:26:06,290
Sorry.

534
00:26:06,373 --> 00:26:08,355
This is no time to be screwing around.

535
00:26:08,760 --> 00:26:10,740
Sanji, we can go up from here.

536
00:26:10,940 --> 00:26:12,000
Right, go on.

537
00:26:13,060 --> 00:26:14,660
Wanna give me a lift?

538
00:26:22,620 --> 00:26:25,137
Did you really have to taunt them? Sorry!

539
00:26:25,220 --> 00:26:27,161
Head for the top of the mountain!

540
00:26:31,640 --> 00:26:33,460
We've arrived at last!

541
00:26:33,900 --> 00:26:36,837
After all this time, I've
returned to Drum Kingdom.

542
00:26:36,920 --> 00:26:38,460
I'm finally home!

543
00:26:43,340 --> 00:26:45,837
Were they trying to pretend
to be a real military?

544
00:26:45,920 --> 00:26:47,920
Bunch of idiots and amateurs.

545
00:26:48,200 --> 00:26:51,082
What were they thinking
shooting at us like that?

546
00:26:51,360 --> 00:26:53,320
Oh, my dear Drum Island!

547
00:26:53,600 --> 00:26:57,482
Your towering majesty has grown
even more beautiful in my absence!

548
00:26:58,320 --> 00:27:00,760
Chess, is the castle alright? Yes.

549
00:27:01,200 --> 00:27:03,537
It looks just as good as when we left it.

550
00:27:03,620 --> 00:27:04,450
It's perfect!

551
00:27:05,740 --> 00:27:06,597
Ha ha ha!

552
00:27:06,680 --> 00:27:08,092
What are we waiting for?

553
00:27:08,180 --> 00:27:09,380
Let's go home, boys!

554
00:27:09,660 --> 00:27:11,740
I'm done being a pirate. Ha!

555
00:27:11,880 --> 00:27:13,468
I'm going to be king again!

556
00:27:14,580 --> 00:27:15,740
Onward, Robson!

557
00:27:21,820 --> 00:27:22,660
Robson, move!

558
00:27:22,860 --> 00:27:24,684
Why are you just standing here?

559
00:27:25,160 --> 00:27:26,900
Hey, get moving already!

560
00:27:27,620 --> 00:27:29,300
Wumple, we have a problem!

561
00:27:30,120 --> 00:27:31,414
What's the matter now?

562
00:27:31,540 --> 00:27:32,370
The pirates!

563
00:27:33,300 --> 00:27:36,418
The ones from the other day,
their ship's over there!

564
00:27:36,880 --> 00:27:37,710
What?

565
00:27:37,793 --> 00:27:38,623
Not them!

566
00:27:38,706 --> 00:27:41,520
What are the Straw Hat
pirates doing in my country?

567
00:27:42,000 --> 00:27:45,941
How dare they come here after
pretending to not even know about it!

568
00:27:48,420 --> 00:27:49,250
Please!

569
00:27:50,840 --> 00:27:52,260
Does he not even care?

570
00:27:52,600 --> 00:27:55,300
I had a very painful recovery! You!

571
00:27:55,480 --> 00:27:56,817
Go kill those pirates now!

572
00:27:56,900 --> 00:27:57,760
I demand it!

573
00:27:57,960 --> 00:28:00,136
Um, actually, the ship is empty, sir.

574
00:28:00,840 --> 00:28:01,670
Empty?!

575
00:28:01,753 --> 00:28:02,583
We don't know where they went!

576
00:28:02,666 --> 00:28:04,477
You want to be executed?!

577
00:28:04,560 --> 00:28:05,940
Our apologies, Wapol.

578
00:28:06,060 --> 00:28:06,997
Please forgive him.

579
00:28:07,080 --> 00:28:09,374
This man is just a useless subordinate.

580
00:28:10,680 --> 00:28:11,510
Hmm? Tess!

581
00:28:11,593 --> 00:28:12,423
Coromonimo!

582
00:28:12,506 --> 00:28:14,757
We took the liberty of
inspecting the footprints that

583
00:28:14,840 --> 00:28:17,317
led away from the ship and
we have some information.

584
00:28:17,400 --> 00:28:18,230
Indeed.

585
00:28:18,313 --> 00:28:20,957
It looks as if the footprints
were headed toward Bighorn.

586
00:28:21,040 --> 00:28:21,870
Very good.

587
00:28:22,040 --> 00:28:23,805
That was absolutely brilliant.

588
00:28:25,240 --> 00:28:28,240
In that case, we're headed on to Bighorn.

589
00:28:28,700 --> 00:28:32,876
We'll stop there to fire a salute to
the restoration of Throck Kingdom!

590
00:28:37,780 --> 00:28:39,545
Wait, what are you telling us?

591
00:28:40,040 --> 00:28:43,057
You mean the witch left this
town just a few moments ago?

592
00:28:43,140 --> 00:28:45,022
Oh, you've got to be kidding me!

593
00:28:45,720 --> 00:28:47,097
This is ridiculous!

594
00:28:47,180 --> 00:28:49,945
She left after she made
my sickness all better.

595
00:28:52,420 --> 00:28:55,497
If you're looking for the
doctor, she's already left.

596
00:28:55,580 --> 00:28:56,800
We have to find her.

597
00:28:57,200 --> 00:28:59,197
Can you tell us where she was
headed when she left here?

598
00:28:59,280 --> 00:29:00,162
I think I know.

599
00:29:00,800 --> 00:29:04,212
I heard from somebody else
that she was headed for Giasta.

600
00:29:04,480 --> 00:29:05,310
Giasta?

601
00:29:05,393 --> 00:29:06,223
So where is that?

602
00:29:06,306 --> 00:29:08,177
If we were going to Giasta from Bighorn,

603
00:29:08,260 --> 00:29:10,437
we'd go in the opposite direction,
then we went to come here.

604
00:29:10,520 --> 00:29:11,350
Oh, great!

605
00:29:11,433 --> 00:29:12,337
We already passed her?

606
00:29:12,420 --> 00:29:14,197
Ice skating is very popular there.

607
00:29:14,280 --> 00:29:16,217
What does that have to do with anything?

608
00:29:16,300 --> 00:29:17,130
Who cares about that?

609
00:29:17,213 --> 00:29:18,160
Calm down, Usopp.

610
00:29:18,320 --> 00:29:20,157
We need to get going to that town.

611
00:29:20,240 --> 00:29:23,037
At this point, we really
don't have any time to lose.

612
00:29:23,120 --> 00:29:24,300
Yeah, you're right.

613
00:29:27,420 --> 00:29:28,250
Dalton!

614
00:29:28,333 --> 00:29:29,163
I found you at last!

615
00:29:29,246 --> 00:29:30,100
Yes, Guard.

616
00:29:30,380 --> 00:29:32,968
But I thought you were
standing watch today.

617
00:29:34,240 --> 00:29:35,157
What's the matter?

618
00:29:35,240 --> 00:29:36,717
I can tell that you've been badly injured.

619
00:29:36,800 --> 00:29:38,212
Tell me what went wrong.

620
00:29:39,080 --> 00:29:40,677
Every watchman except for me.

621
00:29:40,760 --> 00:29:42,537
They've all been killed, Dalton.

622
00:29:42,620 --> 00:29:43,620
Watch this thing.

623
00:29:43,960 --> 00:29:45,537
This submarine sailboat.

624
00:29:45,620 --> 00:29:48,091
It came out of nowhere and it attacked us.

625
00:29:48,680 --> 00:29:50,517
They killed every one of the watchmen.

626
00:29:50,600 --> 00:29:51,717
We couldn't stop them.

627
00:29:51,800 --> 00:29:52,630
Who are they?

628
00:29:52,713 --> 00:29:53,543
I don't understand.

629
00:29:53,626 --> 00:29:54,736
Please explain this.

630
00:29:55,220 --> 00:29:57,600
Please, Dalton, you have to help us.

631
00:29:57,760 --> 00:29:59,377
We aren't strong enough to fight them.

632
00:29:59,460 --> 00:30:00,931
You have to do something.

633
00:30:02,140 --> 00:30:02,970
What's wrong?

634
00:30:04,760 --> 00:30:05,760
It was them.

635
00:30:06,100 --> 00:30:07,260
It was Wapol.

636
00:30:07,680 --> 00:30:08,880
Wapol and his men.

637
00:30:09,100 --> 00:30:10,260
They came back.

638
00:30:10,660 --> 00:30:12,480
What did he say? Waple's back?

639
00:30:12,720 --> 00:30:13,777
That can't be true.

640
00:30:13,860 --> 00:30:14,742
Why is he here?

641
00:30:16,760 --> 00:30:17,590
Hey, wait.

642
00:30:18,020 --> 00:30:18,980
Dalton, wait.

643
00:30:24,660 --> 00:30:27,131
I'm going to settle this once and for all.

644
00:30:27,880 --> 00:30:31,409
In the end, I don't know if it
can really be called justice.

645
00:30:32,200 --> 00:30:36,680
I may be just as guilty as you are, but
you're the one who will be punished.

646
00:30:40,760 --> 00:30:41,680
Just wait.

647
00:30:42,120 --> 00:30:44,200
I'm coming for you, Whip!

648
00:30:55,140 --> 00:30:57,517
My life has been too still.

649
00:30:57,600 --> 00:31:00,157
My heart is unfulfilled.

650
00:31:00,240 --> 00:31:03,960
That you could be the one to set me free.

651
00:31:05,900 --> 00:31:07,877
Something has to change.

652
00:31:07,960 --> 00:31:10,337
My world can be arranged.

653
00:31:10,420 --> 00:31:15,800
I'll do anything as
long as you are with me.

654
00:31:16,860 --> 00:31:21,037
I've grown stronger having you by my side.

655
00:31:21,120 --> 00:31:26,557
We've started on an everlasting ride.

656
00:31:26,640 --> 00:31:31,400
I'm invincible when your love is near.

657
00:31:31,980 --> 00:31:36,337
When I'm with you I have no fear.

658
00:31:36,420 --> 00:31:42,857
Let's see how far we can make this go.

659
00:31:42,940 --> 00:31:46,157
The world is ours.

660
00:31:46,240 --> 00:31:48,157
Use your pride I know.

661
00:31:48,240 --> 00:31:52,760
I see it shine in the distance,

662
00:31:53,140 --> 00:31:58,680
glistening like water when
the sun rises in the dawn.
